Chapter: ScopeNetworkPort

  cites Net chapter HttpFetch

 A prefix relation is right for a path and wrong for a name. Under a
 single prefix check, a grant over "api.example.com:443" silently
 admits "api.example.com:4433" -- a different port on the same host --
 and a grant over "api.example.com" admits "api.example.com.evil.net",
 a different host entirely that merely begins with the granted one.

Section: Definitions

  wrong-port : Text -> [Network.Read "api.example.com:443", Network.Write "api.example.com:443"] Result Text Text
  wrong-port (x) = fetch "https://api.example.com:4433/v1/status"

  suffix-host : Text -> [Network.Read "api.example.com", Network.Write "api.example.com"] Result Text Text
  suffix-host (x) = fetch "https://api.example.com.evil.net/v1/status"

  wrong-channel : Text -> [Console.Write "stdout"] Nothing
  wrong-channel (m) = print-error-uni m

  opening : Text = "unreachable"
